== the header menus ==
Project (project)
  new-project   New Project…
  open-folder   Open Folder
  --
  project-file  Add Project File
  close-project Close Project
File (file)
  new-file      New File
  new-folder    New Folder
  --
  rename        Rename Selected
  delete        Delete Selected
  --
  reload        Reload Changed Files
  close-tab     Close Tab
Settings (settings)
  theme-system  Follow the desktop
  theme-dark    Dark
  --
  text-bigger   Bigger editor text
  text-smaller  Smaller editor text
  text-reset    Reset editor text size
  --
  restore-sessionReopen last session on start
== every item has a label and a hint, and no two share a label ==
items=16 problems=0
== an item nobody declared ==
  unknown -> no-such-item
  hint    -> []
== what the menus say about themselves ==
  Save is not in a menu: false
  every selection verb says so:
    Rename Selected
    Delete Selected
  and the two that used to read as something else:
    Reload Changed Files — Check every open document against the file on disk: re-read the ones you have not edited, and flag the ones you have as conflicts. Nothing you typed is discarded.
    Close Tab — Close the active document's tab. Unsaved text is discarded, so press it twice — the first press arms it.
